.TH PHASORSTD_MEM 3 "August 2026" "Phasor 4.0.0" "Phasor Standard Library 4.0.0"
.SH NAME
phasorstd_mem \- Phasor native memory management functions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBinclude "std/mem.phs";\fR
.PP
.B malloc_native(size)
.B calloc_native(size)
.B realloc_native(handle, size)
.B free_native(handle)
.B c_stralloc_native(data)
.B c_strcpy_native(dest, src)
.B write_native(handle, data)
.B write_offset_native(handle, offset, data)
.B write_c_string_native(handle, data)
.B write_c_string_offset_native(handle, offset, data)
.B read_native(handle)
.B read_native_offset(handle, offset)
.B read_c_string_native(handle)
.B read_c_string_native_offset(handle, offset)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This module exposes raw, unmanaged heap memory to Phasor scripts, for building binary
buffers or interoperating with native data. Every function works in terms of a
.B ManagedMemory
handle (see TYPES) rather than a bare pointer: the handle pairs a native address with the
byte size the allocation was made with, and that size is used as the bound for every
subsequent read or write against the handle.
.PP
There is no garbage collection in this module. Every successful allocation from
.BR malloc_native() ", " calloc_native() ", " realloc_native() ", or " c_stralloc_native()
must eventually be released with exactly one call to \fBfree_native()\fR. Using a handle
after it has been freed, or freeing it twice, is undefined behavior, exactly as with C's
\fBmalloc\fR/\fBfree\fR.
.SH TYPES
.TP
.B ManagedMemory
.RS
.nf
struct ManagedMemory {
    ptr: i64,
    size: i64
}
.fi
.PP
.B ptr
is the native memory address, as an integer.
.B size
is the byte size associated with the allocation, and is what every read/write function in
this module uses to bound its access \(em it is not necessarily how many bytes are still
"valid" after a partial write, just the size of the buffer itself.
.PP
The variable
.B null_managed_memory
is a pre-built \fBManagedMemory\fR with \fBptr: 0\fR and \fBsize: 0\fR, useful as a sentinel
or default value.
.RE
.SH ALLOCATION
.TP
.BR malloc_native (size)
Allocate \fBsize\fR bytes of uninitialized heap memory.
.RS
.PP
.B Arguments:
.RS
.IP \fBsize\fR 12
Number of bytes to allocate; must be greater than zero
.RE
.PP
.B Returns:
A \fBManagedMemory\fR handle with \fBsize\fR set to the requested size
.PP
.B Throws:
Runtime error if \fBsize\fR is not a positive integer, or if the allocation fails
.RE
.PP
.TP
.BR calloc_native (size)
Allocate \fBsize\fR bytes of zero-initialized heap memory.
.RS
.PP
.B Arguments:
.RS
.IP \fBsize\fR 12
Number of bytes to allocate; must be greater than zero
.RE
.PP
.B Returns:
A \fBManagedMemory\fR handle with \fBsize\fR set to the requested size, with every byte
initialized to zero
.PP
.B Throws:
Runtime error if \fBsize\fR is not a positive integer, or if the allocation fails
.RE
.PP
.TP
.BR realloc_native (handle, size)
Resize a previous allocation.
.RS
.PP
.B Arguments:
.RS
.IP \fBhandle\fR 12
A \fBManagedMemory\fR handle previously returned by \fBmalloc_native()\fR,
\fBcalloc_native()\fR, or a prior \fBrealloc_native()\fR call
.IP \fBsize\fR 12
New size in bytes; must be greater than zero
.RE
.PP
.B Returns:
A new \fBManagedMemory\fR handle with \fBsize\fR set to the new size. The underlying address
may or may not change; always use the returned handle, and discard the old one.
.PP
.B Throws:
Runtime error if \fBsize\fR is not a positive integer, or if the reallocation fails
.RE
.PP
.TP
.BR free_native (handle)
Release a heap allocation.
.RS
.PP
.B Arguments:
.RS
.IP \fBhandle\fR 12
A \fBManagedMemory\fR handle previously returned by \fBmalloc_native()\fR,
\fBcalloc_native()\fR, \fBrealloc_native()\fR, or \fBc_stralloc_native()\fR
.RE
.PP
.B Returns:
Null. The handle's memory is freed, but the handle value itself is left unchanged (Phasor
does not null it out); do not read or write through it after this call.
.RE
.SH C STRING HELPERS
.TP
.BR c_stralloc_native (data)
Allocate a null-terminated C string on the heap from a Phasor string.
.RS
.PP
.B Arguments:
.RS
.IP \fBdata\fR 12
String to copy onto the heap
.RE
.PP
.B Returns:
A \fBManagedMemory\fR handle whose \fBsize\fR is \fBlength(data) + 1\fR (the extra byte is
the terminating NUL), containing \fBdata\fR followed by a NUL byte
.PP
.B Throws:
Runtime error if the allocation fails
.RE
.PP
.TP
.BR c_strcpy_native (dest, src)
Copy a null-terminated C string from one allocation into another.
.RS
.PP
.B Arguments:
.RS
.IP \fBdest\fR 12
Destination \fBManagedMemory\fR handle
.IP \fBsrc\fR 12
Source \fBManagedMemory\fR handle; must contain a NUL byte within its \fBsize\fR
.RE
.PP
.B Returns:
Null
.PP
.B Throws:
Runtime error if \fBsrc\fR does not contain a NUL terminator within its recorded size, or if
\fBdest\fR is too small to hold the string being copied (including its NUL terminator)
.RE
.SH RAW READ/WRITE
.TP
.BR write_native (handle, data)
Write an integer into a memory block, as raw bytes.
.RS
.PP
.B Arguments:
.RS
.IP \fBhandle\fR 12
A \fBManagedMemory\fR handle
.IP \fBdata\fR 12
Integer value to write
.RE
.PP
.B Returns:
Null
.PP
.B Notes:
At most 8 bytes (the size of an \fBi64\fR) are written, and never more than
\fBhandle.size\fR bytes; if \fBhandle.size\fR is smaller than 8, only the low-order
\fBhandle.size\fR bytes of \fBdata\fR are written. Byte order follows the host platform's
native endianness.
.RE
.PP
.TP
.BR write_offset_native (handle, offset, data)
Write an integer into a memory block at a byte offset.
.RS
.PP
.B Arguments:
.RS
.IP \fBhandle\fR 12
A \fBManagedMemory\fR handle
.IP \fBoffset\fR 12
Byte offset into the block, from \fB0\fR to \fBhandle.size\fR inclusive
.IP \fBdata\fR 12
Integer value to write
.RE
.PP
.B Returns:
Null
.PP
.B Notes:
Writes at most \fBmin(handle.size \- offset, 8)\fR bytes starting at \fBoffset\fR.
.PP
.B Throws:
Runtime error if \fBoffset\fR is negative or greater than \fBhandle.size\fR
.RE
.PP
.TP
.BR read_native (handle)
Read an integer out of a memory block, as raw bytes.
.RS
.PP
.B Arguments:
.RS
.IP \fBhandle\fR 12
A \fBManagedMemory\fR handle
.RE
.PP
.B Returns:
Integer assembled from at most 8 bytes (never more than \fBhandle.size\fR) read starting at
the beginning of the block, in the host platform's native endianness. Unread high-order bytes
are zero.
.RE
.PP
.TP
.BR read_native_offset (handle, offset)
Read an integer out of a memory block at a byte offset.
.RS
.PP
.B Arguments:
.RS
.IP \fBhandle\fR 12
A \fBManagedMemory\fR handle
.IP \fBoffset\fR 12
Byte offset into the block, from \fB0\fR to \fBhandle.size\fR inclusive
.RE
.PP
.B Returns:
Integer assembled from at most \fBmin(handle.size \- offset, 8)\fR bytes read starting at
\fBoffset\fR
.PP
.B Throws:
Runtime error if \fBoffset\fR is negative or greater than \fBhandle.size\fR
.RE
.SH C STRING READ/WRITE
.TP
.BR write_c_string_native (handle, data)
Write a Phasor string into a memory block as a null-terminated C string.
.RS
.PP
.B Arguments:
.RS
.IP \fBhandle\fR 12
A \fBManagedMemory\fR handle
.IP \fBdata\fR 12
String to write
.RE
.PP
.B Returns:
Null
.PP
.B Notes:
At most \fBhandle.size \- 1\fR characters of \fBdata\fR are copied (silently truncating
longer strings), always leaving room for and writing a terminating NUL byte.
.RE
.PP
.TP
.BR write_c_string_offset_native (handle, offset, data)
Write a Phasor string as a null-terminated C string at a byte offset.
.RS
.PP
.B Arguments:
.RS
.IP \fBhandle\fR 12
A \fBManagedMemory\fR handle
.IP \fBoffset\fR 12
Byte offset into the block, from \fB0\fR to \fBhandle.size\fR
.IP \fBdata\fR 12
String to write
.RE
.PP
.B Returns:
Null
.PP
.B Notes:
At most \fB(handle.size \- offset) \- 1\fR characters of \fBdata\fR are copied, leaving room
for a terminating NUL byte, which is always written.
.PP
.B Throws:
Runtime error if \fBoffset\fR is negative, greater than or equal to \fBhandle.size\fR, or
leaves no room for even a NUL terminator
.RE
.PP
.TP
.BR read_c_string_native (handle)
Read a null-terminated C string out of a memory block.
.RS
.PP
.B Arguments:
.RS
.IP \fBhandle\fR 12
A \fBManagedMemory\fR handle
.RE
.PP
.B Returns:
String read starting at the beginning of the block, stopping at the first NUL byte or after
\fBhandle.size\fR bytes, whichever comes first (a missing NUL terminator is not an error)
.RE
.PP
.TP
.BR read_c_string_native_offset (handle, offset)
Read a null-terminated C string out of a memory block at a byte offset.
.RS
.PP
.B Arguments:
.RS
.IP \fBhandle\fR 12
A \fBManagedMemory\fR handle
.IP \fBoffset\fR 12
Byte offset into the block, from \fB0\fR to \fBhandle.size\fR inclusive
.RE
.PP
.B Returns:
String read starting at \fBoffset\fR, stopping at the first NUL byte or after
\fBhandle.size \- offset\fR bytes, whichever comes first
.PP
.B Throws:
Runtime error if \fBoffset\fR is negative or greater than \fBhandle.size\fR
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.B Basic Allocation
.PP
.nf
.RS
include "std/mem.phs";

var block = malloc_native(8);
write_native(block, 42);
puts(read_native(block));   // 42
free_native(block);

var zeroed = calloc_native(16);
puts(read_native(zeroed));  // 0
free_native(zeroed);
.RE
.fi
.PP
.B C Strings
.PP
.nf
.RS
include "std/mem.phs";

var greeting = c_stralloc_native("hello");
puts(read_c_string_native(greeting));  // "hello"

var copy = malloc_native(greeting.size);
c_strcpy_native(copy, greeting);
puts(read_c_string_native(copy));      // "hello"

free_native(greeting);
free_native(copy);
.RE
.fi
.PP
.B Resizing a Buffer
.PP
.nf
.RS
include "std/mem.phs";

var buf = malloc_native(4);
write_native(buf, 100);
buf = realloc_native(buf, 16);  // reassign; old handle is no longer valid
write_offset_native(buf, 8, 200);
puts(read_native(buf));            // 100
puts(read_native_offset(buf, 8));  // 200
free_native(buf);
.RE
.fi
.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
Every allocating function (\fBmalloc_native()\fR, \fBcalloc_native()\fR,
\fBrealloc_native()\fR, \fBc_stralloc_native()\fR) must be paired with exactly one
\fBfree_native()\fR call; there is no automatic memory management in this module
.IP \(bu 2
.B realloc_native()
returns a new handle; do not continue using the handle you passed in, since its address may
have moved or been freed
.IP \(bu 2
All read/write functions are bounded by the \fBsize\fR recorded in the handle you pass, not
by any size you pass separately \(em to read or write fewer bytes, allocate a smaller block
or use the \fB_offset\fR variants
.IP \(bu 2
The integer read/write functions
.RB ( write_native (), " " read_native () ,
and their
.B _offset
counterparts) cap every access at 8 bytes, the size of an \fBi64\fR
.IP \(bu 2
This module was previously exposed as a simpler, name-based API for freeing VM-managed
values; that API no longer exists. All functions in this module now operate on native
\fBManagedMemory\fR handles as described above.
